 "notes": "No feature in the unit's own row (S2430) or in its SWP entry (Mem III, Tell es Samarat: mound only). SWP 'Khurbet es Sumrah' (square Ot, 8.2 km) is a different place; no features; ignored. N82 (Tell es-Samarat, 25 m) is a separate Nigro point; its tombs take grid N82. E/S duplicate rows of one site (E343, E344, E349, E335, E336, E327, E332, E333, E331, E328, E329, E330, E324, E359, E320, E360, E363) recorded once per source. S2350 (terrace of the Cave of the Sandal) treated as the same cave as S2351. Natural caves, cavities and passages coded as pits; recesses, niches, fissures, rock shelters and the cliff not coded. Human bones / 38 skeletons in S2341, S2342, S2339, S2350 not coded as graves (no burial stated). Avi'or Cave (S2342) and E325 (empty components) coded as caves from the row name. N47 has no coordinates in the packet: position none. N21 nympheum (Roman) not coded as a pool; N85 rock-cut ditch, N75 water supply system/moat not coded. N7 pits dated 2nd century AD coded U. No explicit absence statements."
}